# Development Tools

## Testing

### Unit Tests

- Unit tests for helpers, composables, or components in isolation.
- Co-locate with file under test: `[NameOfComponent].unit.spec.ts`.
- Use `@vue/test-utils`.
- Quality over quantity.

### E2E Tests

- Add `data-testid` to all interactive elements (buttons, links, inputs, selects, modals, toggles).
- Follow the dot-notation convention defined in `data-testid-convention.mdc`: `domain.component.element-type` e.g. `auth.login-form.email-input`, `nav.sidebar.home-link`, `employees.list.add-btn`.
- `data-testid` must be stable and not derived from dynamic content (no IDs, indices, or user-generated strings).
- E2E tests live in `e2e/`. Use Playwright selectors via `getByTestId()`.

## Node / JS / TypeScript

- Use npm for package management.

## Typing and Linting

- Prettier for formatting (`npm run format` / `npx prettier --write <files>`).
- ESLint (`npm run lint` / `npx eslint <files> --fix`). CI uses `npm run lint:ci`.
- After edits, format and lint **touched files** before finishing. See `development.mdc` After Every Edit.
- `vitest/expect-expect` requires `expect()` in the test body. Do not hide assertions in helpers — the rule will fail in CI.
- Do not use type `any`.
